zlib — via github.com/cwbudde/go-absolute-database (internal/zlib1)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

SoundPLAN's .abs files store their compressed internal structures as C zlib
level-1 streams, and reproducing them byte for byte requires zlib's own
deflate_fast encoder, which Go's compress/flate does not implement. That
dependency therefore carries an ALTERED Go port of zlib 1.2.13's deflate.c and
trees.c, plainly marked as altered. It is not zlib: it is a Go rewrite, it
implements level 1 only, and it compresses but does not decompress. Report any
defect in it to Aconiq or to go-absolute-database, never to the zlib authors.

